{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Field","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Power","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.omegaFactor_antitone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.omegaFactor_antitone","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L173-L193","doc":"Each factor of the Ω-quotient on the counting circle `|u| = w⁻¹` is\nantitone in `S = sin²(θ/2)`.  With `x = w^{2i+1}` the factor is\n`((1 − wx)² + 4wx·S) / ((1 − x)² + 4x·S)`; monotonicity follows from\n`omega_factor_key`, whose right-hand side is negative for `0 < w < 1`,\n`0 < x < 1`.  Evaluating at `S = 0` therefore majorises the whole circle,\nwhich is what turns the Rouché threshold `n₀(w)` into a closed-form,\ngrid-free quantity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.omega_factor_key","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.omega_factor_key","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L167-L171","doc":"The algebraic heart of the counting-circle majorant:\n`w(1−x)² − (1−wx)² = −(1−w)(1 − wx²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.prod_one_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.prod_one_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L151-L163","doc":"Product form of the reflection identity: the finite telescoping used to\nevaluate the even-`j` ratio in closed form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.one_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.one_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L144-L149","doc":"`1 − x⁻¹ = −x⁻¹ (1 − x)`.  Applied with `x = w^{2i} u` this is the exact\ncancellation that collapses the even-`j` defect ratio to `w^{−s(s+1)}|u|^{−s}`,\nkeeping the theta cancellation in the Rouché comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.tropRoot_lt_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.tropRoot_lt_succ","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L123-L140","doc":"The tropical roots are strictly increasing for `0 < w < 1`: the Newton\npolygon of `A_w` is strictly convex, so every corner is a genuine corner and\ndistinct indices give distinct tropical roots.  The whole statement reduces to\n`w^{n+2} < 1 + w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.tropRoot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.tropRoot","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L120-L121","doc":"The `n`-th tropical root `w^{−(2n+1)}(1 − w^{n+1})` of `A_w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L105-L116","doc":"Division-free form of the coefficient ratio of `A_w`.  Writing\n`a_n = (−1)^n w^{n²}/(w;w)_n`, this says `a_n / a_{n+1} = −w^{−(2n+1)}(1−w^{n+1})`,\ni.e. the `n`-th tropical root is `w^{−(2n+1)}(1 − w^{n+1})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch_succ","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L102-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch_zero","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.wPoch","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L95-L98","doc":"`(w;w)_n = ∏_{i=1}^{n} (1 - w^i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.recentring_zpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.recentring_zpow","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L87-L91","doc":"The field-level form of `recentring_exponent`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.recentring_exponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.AwZeroLocalization.recentring_exponent","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/AwZeroLocalization.lean#L79-L85","doc":"The Gaussian exponent of `A_w` recentres at index `n` under the\nsubstitution `z = w^{1−2n} u`:  `m² + (1−2n)m = (n − n²) + (m−n)(m−n+1)`.\nThe right-hand side is a constant plus a Gaussian in `m − n`, so the term of\nindex `m = n` is the extremal one at that argument. ","signatureChunk":0}]}